&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a scalable product enablement program for GTM teams (Initially the focus will be Sales, but can expand and overlap to SEs/SAs, Customer Outcomes, Support, Partnerships), covering launches, core product foundations, advanced AI capabilities, and platform‑level narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver high‑impact enablement sessions on new features, packages, and workflows, with a focus on active practice, demos, and application to real customer scenarios, not just slides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Product Marketing, Competitive, Sales, Technical Enablement, and Customer Outcomes to ensure GTM teams are launch‑ready for Tier 1 and Tier 2 releases, with clear talk tracks, demo flows, objection handling, and enablement bundles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Field and Technical Enablement peers to embed product learning into broader programs such as onboarding, certifications, deal coaching, and manager enablement, so product knowledge shows up in how we sell and support, not just in standalone trainings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operate an AI‑first “launch‑to‑enable” loop: help define how product changes (release notes, docs, support patterns) become structured launch briefs, role‑based guidance, and in‑flow practice using Glean and agents as the backbone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technical Enablement and AI product teams to build and maintain AI‑powered enablement surfaces (e.g., role‑aware “what’s new” views, browser‑overlay guidance, agent‑driven labs) that deliver just‑in‑time coaching in the tools where GTM already works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a champion and co‑designer of our AI‑first enablement system by collaborating on 30‑/60‑/90‑day MVPs (e.g., an enablement‑owned launch hub, role‑aware readiness signals, agent‑assisted certifications) and feeding field feedback back into our AI enablement roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About you:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in B2B SaaS go‑to‑market roles such as product enablement, sales/revenue enablement, product marketing, solutions engineering, or similar roles with heavy product ownership and field interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record translating complex, technical, or AI‑heavy product concepts into simple, compelling narratives, talk tracks, and trainings that GTM teams actually use in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with modern value‑based sales methodologies (e.g., Command of the Message, MEDDICC/MEDDPICC, or similar) and how product stories must align to business problems, outcomes, and proof points, not just features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of how AI products work at a conceptual level (e.g., large language models, retrieval‑augmented generation, knowledge graphs, security and permissions), even if you are not a deep technical expert, and curiosity about how Work AI changes selling and customer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands‑on experience using AI tools to design, deliver, or scale enablement, for example, using AI to draft curricula, build interactive labs, power self‑serve Q&amp;amp;A, or run lightweight, agent‑assisted certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and program management skills: able to juggle multiple launches, stakeholder groups, and content streams while keeping timelines, dependencies, and success metrics clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity and a high‑change environment, you can keep up with a fast product release cadence, find signal in the noise, and quickly determine what the field actually needs versus what would be “nice to have.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker who gets excited about turning one‑off trainings into durable, AI‑powered enablement experiences, you think in terms of loops, signals, and workflows, not just events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is hybrid (4 days a week in one of our New York City office location)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard base salary range for this position is $140,000 - $187,000 annually. Compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for variable compensation, equity, and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a comprehensive benefits package including competitive compensation, Medical, Vision, and Dental coverage, generous time-off policy, and the opportunity to contribute to your 401k plan to support your long-term goals. When you join, you&#39;ll receive a home office improvement stipend, as well as an annual education and wellness stipends to support your growth and wellbeing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a diverse bunch of people and we want to continue to attract and retain a diverse range of people into our organization. We&#39;re committed to an inclusive and diverse company. We do not discriminate based on gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, civil or family status, age, disability, or race.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-First Mindset at Glean:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At Glean, AI fluency is core to how we work and we&#39;re committed to ensuring every new hire feels confident integrating AI into their everyday work. &lt;strong&gt;As part of the interview process, you&#39;ll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about, design, and use AI to drive impact in your role. &lt;/strong&gt;Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today — prior Glean experience isn&#39;t required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Data Privacy Notice for Job Candidates and Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Depending on your location, the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), or other privacy laws may regulate the way we manage the data of job applicants. Our full notice outlining how data will be processed as part of the application procedure for applicable locations is available in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.glean.com/privacy&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. By submitting your application, you are agreeing to our use and processing of your data as required. US applicants and their applications are subject to arbitration of disputes as outlined in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.glean.com/arbitrationagreement&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Arbitration Agreement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;By clicking “Submit Application,” I confirm that I have read the Global Data Privacy Notice and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.glean.com/arbitrationagreement&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Arbitration Agreement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and I agree to the terms.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Glean:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Glean is the Work AI platform that helps everyone work smarter with AI. What began as the industry’s most advanced enterprise search has evolved into a full-scale Work AI ecosystem, powering intelligent Search, an AI Assistant, and scalable AI agents on one secure, open platform. With over 100 enterprise SaaS connectors, flexible LLM choice, and robust APIs, Glean gives organizations the infrastructure to govern, scale, and customize AI across their entire business - without vendor lock-in or costly implementation cycles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At its core, Glean is redefining how enterprises find, use, and act on knowledge. Its Enterprise Graph and Personal Knowledge Graph map the relationships between people, content, and activity, delivering deeply personalized, context-aware responses for every employee. This foundation powers Glean’s agentic capabilities - AI agents that automate real work across teams by accessing the industry’s broadest range of data: enterprise and world, structured and unstructured, historical and real-time. The result: measurable business impact through faster onboarding, hours of productivity gained each week, and smarter, safer decisions at every level.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Recognized by Fast Company as one of the World’s Most Innovative Companies (Top 10, 2025), by CNBC’s Disruptor 50, Bloomberg’s AI Startups to Watch (2026), Forbes AI 50, and Gartner’s Tech Innovators in Agentic AI, Glean continues to accelerate its global impact. With customers across 50+ industries and 1,000+ employees in more than 25 countries, we’re helping the world’s largest organizations make every employee AI-fluent, and turning the superintelligent enterprise from concept into reality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;If you’re excited to shape how the world works, you’ll help build systems used daily across Microsoft Teams, Zoom, ServiceNow, Zendesk, GitHub, and many more. You&#39;ll be deeply embedded where people get things done. You&#39;ll ship agentic capabilities on an open, extensible stack, with the craft and care required for enterprise trust, as we bring Work AI to every employee, in every company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Glean is at an inflection point where product decisions carry real P&amp;amp;L consequences&amp;nbsp; from AI infrastructure costs to consumption-based pricing models. We&#39;re looking for a highly analytical and strategic Product Finance Analyst to partner closely with Product, Engineering, GTM, and Leadership teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;This role will help drive investment decisions, pricing and monetization strategy, unit economics analysis, and long-range planning for Glean&#39;s rapidly growing AI and product offerings. You will play a key role in translating product strategy into financial insights and helping leadership make data-driven decisions on where and how to scale the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering leaders to evaluate product investments, roadmap prioritization, and resource allocation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain financial models for new products, AI usage economics, and infrastructure cost forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze product-level revenue performance, customer adoption trends, and margin drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pricing, packaging, and monetization analyses across SaaS and AI consumption-based offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop dashboards and KPI reporting for leadership reviews and operating cadences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM and Revenue Operations teams on customer profitability and expansion analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive annual planning, forecasting, and long-range strategic planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build cost-per-query models for LLM and cloud infrastructure spend and surface actionable optimization opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve financial processes, reporting automation, and decision-making frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, investment banking, consulting, or product finance at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Product and Engineering organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SaaS business models and cloud/software infrastructure economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/LLM cost structures, usage-based pricing, or cloud infrastructure economics is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-first mindset — actively uses AI tools (e.g., Glean, ChatGPT, Cursor) to automate analyses, draft models, and accelerate research workflows, not just basic awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and BigQuery skills; experience with BI tools or financial planning systems is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced and ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting product-led growth (PLG) or AI-native products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of consumption-based revenue models and overage mechanics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to cloud cost allocation (GCP, AWS, Azure) or FinOps practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to SQL and basic scripting to analyze large datasets and support data-driven decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup or high-growth SaaS experience where you&#39;ve owned end-to-end financial modeling with limited guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
