&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;If you’re excited to shape how the world works, you’ll help build systems used daily across Microsoft Teams, Zoom, ServiceNow, Zendesk, GitHub, and many more. You&#39;ll be deeply embedded where people get things done. You&#39;ll ship agentic capabilities on an open, extensible stack, with the craft and care required for enterprise trust, as we bring Work AI to every employee, in every company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Glean is seeking a Senior Sales Recruiter to own full-cycle recruiting across multiple levels and functions within our go-to-market organization. Must have 5+ years of full cycle recruiting experience. You’ll serve as a trusted recruiting partner to Sales leaders, building strong talent pipelines, calibrating hiring profiles, and running a rigorous, data-informed process from intake through close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a recruiter who can move comfortably between strategic partnership and hands-on execution, bring structure to complex searches, and consistently deliver high-quality candidate experiences in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You will:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for multiple levels of GTM roles across Sales, Customer Success, and Solutions/Pre-Sales, from intake and market mapping through sourcing, assessment, closing, and offer acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring leaders to define success profiles, calibrate must-have and trainable signals, establish interview plans, and align on decision criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build role-specific TAMs and prioritized sourcing strategies across target companies, talent communities, geographies, referrals, and direct outreach channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, assess, and close candidates with a high bar for judgment, candidate experience, communication, and alignment to Glean’s values and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead recruiting processes with operational rigor, including clear stage definitions, timely feedback, strong data hygiene, and effective use of Greenhouse, LinkedIn Recruiter, Gem, Modern Loop, and related tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hiring leaders with actionable pipeline insights, including source mix, stage movement, pass-through rates, representation, risks, and recommended interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve GTM recruiting systems, playbooks, calibration practices, and team operating rhythms as the organization scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally hiring across multiple GTM functions and levels in a high-growth B2B SaaS, technology, or similarly complex environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong command of GTM talent profiles, including Sales, Customer Success, and Solutions/Pre-Sales roles, and can identify the signals that predict success in each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are skilled at building TAMs, developing targeted sourcing strategies, and converting market insights into qualified, diverse slates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring sound recruiting judgment and can balance speed, quality, candidate experience, and business priorities in ambiguous or changing conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a strong consultative partner who can influence hiring leaders, facilitate calibration, and communicate clear recommendations backed by evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are metrics-oriented and operationally disciplined, with a track record of maintaining clean processes and using data to improve recruiting outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are energized by building in a fast-paced environment and enjoy making recruiting better for candidates, hiring teams, and fellow recruiters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Location:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is hybrid (3-4 days a week in the Nashville office.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for variable compensation, equity, and benefits.The standard base salary range for this position depends on your leveling, Senior Recruiter $140,000-$170,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We offer a comprehensive benefits package including competitive compensation, Medical, Vision, and Dental coverage, generous time-off policy, and the opportunity to contribute to your 401k plan to support your long-term goals. When you join, you&#39;ll receive a home office improvement stipend, as well as an annual education and wellness stipends to support your growth and wellbeing. We foster a vibrant company culture through regular events, and provide healthy lunches daily to keep you fueled and focused.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are a diverse bunch of people and we want to continue to attract and retain a diverse range of people into our organization. We&#39;re committed to an inclusive and diverse company. We do not discriminate based on gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, civil or family status, age, disability, or race.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
